@@ -105,6 +105,8 @@ At the first eligible `agent/pre-step` of a session, the plugin composes the bas
 
 Every injected message carries a typed source with its change list; a complete baseline also carries an identity derived from normalized discovery, precedence, project-root, and budget configuration, and a matching durable message confirms a queued baseline. Model-visible text contains no hidden state markers, and literal `</system-reminder>` text anywhere in instruction content or model-visible metadata is escaped so repository-controlled text cannot close the plugin-owned frame.
 
+`candidateSelection: first` selects one non-empty candidate per directory for both baseline injection and refresh. Confirmed empty files allow fallthrough; an unavailable higher-priority candidate does not. Winner changes remove the old instruction and set the new one in one durable context batch. `fileTouchToolNames` maps deployment tool names to the existing reconciliation path. Defaults retain all candidates and the stock tool names.
+
 </details>
 
